> Decision: This is a genuine piecewise projection; no production WorkingState/tick fold exists.
> CreateSaucer geometry is materialized only from a visible journal entry; ReferenceContext carries the fixed radius definition.
> Unsupported visible CreateSaucer radii return ProjectionError through try_state and are rejected during persistence decoding.
> Authored same-tick terrain events precede derived events, preserving journal append order before the fixed derived source order.
> The actor layer is projected collectively across live tick transitions with spawn visibility, removals, movement proposals, conflicts, and collisions.
> Selected pieces carry immutable visible journal inputs and a projection regime; rule calculation remains query-local.
> The legacy comparison is owned by discontinuity-parity and is not claimed as universal equivalence.
